<p>+1,great job. However, I am an asshole, so I will say that I noticed the following in your article:</p>
<p>&quot;Approximately two hours after this interview concluded, SCP-5996 was given its official designation. Approximately four hours after that, it was moved into its current containment chamber.&quot;</p>
<p>To me, this phrase seems a little clunky, and I'm not sure to recommend you remove it, or recommend you rewrite it. It just doesn't sit well with me.</p>
<p>My other minor nitpick is that in one of your logs a normal foundation employee casually references the existence of Thaumiels. Very few people are even supposed to know the object class exists, much less actually be able to reference it to lower level staff. If that was in an interview like this, the entire interview probably would be redacted, since most foundation employees are only supposed to know of three object classes.</p>
<p>Again, great work though.</p>

